I kept your flow: one query, strip every non-digit/non-`+` character, leave blank phones out of the update, one partial save after the loop, and a map of failed Id to the first error message.

Two security changes, because this writes customer phone data: the class is `with sharing`, and the query and update run in user mode. `Database.update(contacts, false, AccessLevel.USER_MODE)` is still a single partial save, but CRUD/FLS failures come back on `SaveResult` instead of a silent system-mode write. Failed rows are paired by index because that stays correct even when `SaveResult.getId()` is null. A null or empty id list returns an empty map and does not query. Extra `+` signs are not rearranged — you specified a character filter only.

