The callout cannot run inside the trigger, and it cannot be one request per account. Salesforce rejects HTTP callouts in trigger context, so the trigger only enqueues one Queueable (`Database.AllowsCallouts`) that runs after the insert commits. One callout per account is not bulk-safe: a marketplace insert of 200 would exceed the 100-callout limit and the async-job limit (50 per sync transaction, 1 from Batch/Queueable/future). The ERP already accepts 1–200 customers per POST, which matches the trigger batch size, and each account remains traceable by its 18-character `salesforceId`. One POST per insert transaction is the bulk-safe design.

