/**
 * Sets Account.Rating from that account's open opportunities:
 * Hot  — at least one open opportunity with Amount >= 100,000
 * Warm — one or more open opportunities, none that large
 * Cold — no open opportunities
 *
 * Open means IsClosed = false, so custom closed stages are honored.
 * without sharing: the rollup must see the full pipeline, not only
 * opportunities visible to the user who saved the opportunity.
 */
public without sharing class AccountRatingService {
    private static final Decimal HOT_THRESHOLD = 100000;
    private static Boolean isApplying = false;

    /**
     * Recalculates Rating for every account in the set.
     * One @future for the whole set. Runs inline from batch or future
     * context, where enqueueing another future is not allowed.
     */
    public static void recalculate(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        Set<Id> ids = sanitize(accountIds);
        if (ids.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }
        if (System.isFuture() || System.isBatch()) {
            applyRatings(ids);
            return;
        }
        recalculateAsync(new List<Id>(ids));
    }

    @future
    public static void recalculateAsync(List<Id> accountIds) {
        applyRatings(accountIds == null ? new Set<Id>() : new Set<Id>(accountIds));
    }

    private static void applyRatings(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        if (isApplying) {
            return;
        }
        accountIds = sanitize(accountIds);
        if (accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        isApplying = true;
        try {
            Map<Id, Decimal> maxOpenAmountByAccountId = new Map<Id, Decimal>();
            for (AggregateResult ar : [
                SELECT AccountId, MAX(Amount) maxAmount
                FROM Opportunity
                WHERE AccountId IN :accountIds
                AND IsClosed = false
                GROUP BY AccountId
            ]) {
                maxOpenAmountByAccountId.put(
                    (Id) ar.get('AccountId'),
                    (Decimal) ar.get('maxAmount')
                );
            }

            List<Account> accountsToUpdate = new List<Account>();
            for (Account acc : [SELECT Id, Rating FROM Account WHERE Id IN :accountIds]) {
                Boolean hasOpenOpportunity = maxOpenAmountByAccountId.containsKey(acc.Id);
                String newRating = ratingFor(
                    maxOpenAmountByAccountId.get(acc.Id),
                    hasOpenOpportunity
                );
                if (acc.Rating != newRating) {
                    acc.Rating = newRating;
                    accountsToUpdate.add(acc);
                }
            }

            if (!accountsToUpdate.isEmpty()) {
                update accountsToUpdate;
            }
        } finally {
            isApplying = false;
        }
    }

    private static String ratingFor(Decimal maxOpenAmount, Boolean hasOpenOpportunity) {
        if (!hasOpenOpportunity) {
            return 'Cold';
        }
        // MAX ignores nulls; a null max means every open amount is null.
        if (maxOpenAmount != null && maxOpenAmount >= HOT_THRESHOLD) {
            return 'Hot';
        }
        return 'Warm';
    }

    private static Set<Id> sanitize(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        Set<Id> ids = new Set<Id>();
        if (accountIds != null) {
            ids.addAll(accountIds);
            ids.remove(null);
        }
        return ids;
    }
}
```

What I changed, and why:

- **One `@future` per chunk, not per opportunity.** A transaction may enqueue only 50 future methods. CPQ batches of 200 would throw `System.LimitException: Too many future calls: 51` on the 51st opportunity. The future also runs after commit, so it queries the saved pipeline rather than trusting trigger values. Passing ids (not Opportunity records) is required because `@future` cannot take sObjects.
- **Delete, undelete, and AccountId change are included.** Insert plus StageName/Amount changes alone leave Rating stale when an open opportunity is deleted, restored, or moved to another account. Both the old and new account are recalculated on reparent. Other updates (CloseDate, Description, and so on) do not enqueue work.
- **Inline fallback in batch or future context.** `@future` cannot be called from batch or future Apex. If CPQ's "batches of 200" are Batch Apex, the enqueue would fail the save; the same bulk recalc then runs in that transaction instead. Synchronous UI/API saves still return immediately.
- **`without sharing` and a single aggregate query.** Rating is an account-level fact. `with sharing` would let a user who cannot see a 100k opportunity downgrade a Hot account. `MAX(Amount)` plus `IsClosed = false` decides Hot/Warm/Cold without loading every opportunity. Accounts whose Rating is already correct are not updated.

The per-line `PricingRules.standardDiscountFor` call cannot be used as written: it queries `Product2` once per line, so a 200-line CPQ quote blows the 100-SOQL limit. `PricingRules` stays unchanged and its percentages are not copied. The handler bulk-loads `Family` once and calls `PricingRules.standardDiscountForFamily`, and it only fills `Discount` when it is null (0 is left alone).

