The one-job-per-case enqueue is not safe here, so the trigger enqueues a single job for the whole transaction instead. A transaction can close 200 Cases, but `System.enqueueJob` allows only 50 calls synchronously and 1 from async Apex. Exceeding that throws `LimitException` and rolls back the Case close. The job re-checks `IsClosed` and `ContactId`, then inserts Tasks with `allOrNone=false` so one Task failure does not undo the others. It is `without sharing` because this is a system side effect, and it implements `Database.AllowsCallouts` so the planned vendor callout can be added here (callout before the Task DML).

